  "id": "partial-reinforcement",
  "term": "partial reinforcement",
  "definition": "Partial reinforcement is a learning schedule in which a behavior is rewarded only some of the time rather than after every correct response. Compared with continuous reinforcement, behavior learned this way often persists longer when rewards stop.",
